course: dictionary
lesson: 1765
title: The clef
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clef is a sign at the start of a line of written music. It tells you how high or low the notes on that line are. Without a clef, you would not know which note each line and space stands for.
explain: «Notes sit both on the lines and in the spaces between them; a clef at the start tells you which line is which note.» So the clef is the key you read first, before any notes.
explain: The treble clef is for higher notes, used for recorder, violin and the right hand on the piano. The bass clef is for lower notes, used for low instruments and the left hand. Silly sayings like FACE help you learn the spaces until you just know them.
fact: A clef is a sign at the start of a line of music.
fact: A clef shows how high or low the notes are.
fact: «The treble clef is also called the G clef, because its curl wraps around the line for the note G.»
fact: The treble clef is for higher notes, and the bass clef is for lower notes.
exercise: What does a clef show at the start of a line of music? | The name of the song | *How high or low the notes are | How fast to play | How loud the music should be
exercise: «The treble clef is also called the G clef, because its curl wraps around the line for the note G.» Why is it called the G clef? | Because it is played on a guitar | Because it is the first sign in the book | Because it starts with the letter G | *Because its curl wraps around the line for the note G
exercise: Which clef is used for low instruments and the left hand on the piano? | Recorder clef | Treble clef | *Bass clef | Violin clef
test: «In the treble clef the four spaces from bottom to top are F, A, C and E.» Which notes are in the spaces? | A, B, C and D | E, G, B and D | G, B, D and F | *F, A, C and E
test: In the treble clef, the five lines from bottom to top are E, G, B, D and F. Which note is on the bottom line? | F | *E | G | D
exam: Why is the treble clef also called the G clef? | Because it is only used for guitars | Because it is the first sign in every book | *Because its curl wraps around the line for the note G | Because G is the lowest note on the piano
